  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards UNESCO Biosphere Observatories: A Feasibility Study Exploring IOC systems and Flanders Technology</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This feasibility study for the UNESCO BiOES project addresses global marine reserve monitoring gaps and underutilized data. Its purpose is to assess needs and capacities to deliver technology and skills by leveraging UNESCO-IOC&apos;s advanced global ocean data systems (e.g., OBIS, OTGA, ODIS) and Flanders&apos; marine science expertise. This advises a larger BiOES project to enhance ocean health and resilience, gathering data for early-warning systems. Key activities include desktop studies and interviews assessing IOC/Flanders capacity, culminating in an Ostend stakeholder workshop. Deliverables are assessments and a final report with recommendations.</narrative>
  </description>
